# Command: SDD Resume

Command: /sdd-resume
Mode: SUPERVISED
Purpose: Resume chain execution from last checkpoint

Description:
  Resumes a failed or interrupted chain execution from the
  last successful checkpoint. Skips completed stages and
  continues from where execution stopped.

Usage:
  /sdd-resume
  /sdd-resume --chain=<chain-id>
  /sdd-resume --checkpoint=<checkpoint-id>
  /sdd-resume --list

Options:
  --chain=<id>        Resume specific chain
  --checkpoint=<id>   Resume from specific checkpoint
  --list              List available checkpoints
  --force             Skip confirmation

Resume Process:
  1. Load latest checkpoint (or specified)
  2. Verify checkpoint integrity
  3. Identify last successful stage
  4. Skip completed stages
  5. Resume from next stage
  6. Continue chain execution

Checkpoint Validation:
  - Checkpoint hash matches
  - Stage outputs are valid
  - Dependencies are met
  - No conflicting state

Safety:
  - Current state backed up before resume
  - Human confirmation required
  - Resume logged in audit trail
  - Can abort and restore if needed

Exit Codes:
  0 - Resume successful
  1 - Resume failed
  2 - No checkpoint found
  3 - Checkpoint corrupted

State: +
